+Enterprise-scale runbook (summary)
+
+Purpose
+- Provide operator steps and pointers to turn existing Aegis scaffolds into a production-scale AIOps / MLOps platform.
+
+Key steps
+1) Provision GPU node pool with Cluster Autoscaler using infra/terraform/cluster_autoscaler_nodepool.tf and run ops/gpu/deploy_cluster_autoscaler.sh. Configure provider-specific flags and IAM roles.  
+2) Deploy KEDA + Redis queue to autoscale sim-runner workers and use argo/workflows/longtail_sim_advanced.yaml to orchestrate large sim batches. Provision spot pool using ops/gpu/spot_pool_manager.py.  
+3) Harden and onboard builders: run ops/ci/builder_hardening_and_onboard.sh on each builder host, label them, and configure KMS/OIDC. Verify via ops/ci/verify_builder_provenance_check.py in CI.  
+4) Operationalize RT & HIL across fleet: maintain conf/hw_targets_exact.yaml and run ops/hil/fleet_orchestrator.py to produce signed evidence bundles. Hook into .github/workflows/rt_hil_apalache.yml.  
+5) Incident automation: deploy ops/incident/pagerduty_forwarder.py integration and wire .github/workflows/hil_failure_alert_and_remediate.yml into CI to auto-ticket and page on critical failures.  
+6) Measurement: push PoA metrics with ops/metrics/metric_mapper.py to a Pushgateway and import ops/metrics/grafana_dashboard_template.json into Grafana.  
+
+Notes & cautions
+- Many scripts are provider-agnostic templates: operator must replace cloud-specific bits (Terraform provider blocks, cloud CLI calls, IAM roles).  
+- Ensure KMS/OIDC is fully configured before marking provenance gates enforced in production CI.  
+- Test spot/pretpmptable pools with non-critical sim runs first to ensure autoscaling behavior and preemption handling.
